    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0834" n="820" xml:id="pg820"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis, Acting
                        Secretary of State, to Mr. Boutwell,
                        Secretary of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 28, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[119]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Confidential information has come to this
                    Department that there is some reason to apprehend that the proprietors of the
                    British brig Edith, now at New Orleans, are about to attempt a violation of *the
                    neutrality laws of the United States, by engaging in an armed expedition against
                    the Spanish authorities in Cuba. The informant does not desire to have his name
                    disclosed, and the information he gives is vague and imperfect. Will you have
                    the goodness to instruct the proper officials under your directions by telegraph
                    to watch the vessel carefully, and to ascertain if there be anything suspicious
                    in her preparations, and, if they have reason to believe that she is about to
                    engage in an unlawful occupation, to take the necessary steps to prevent her
                    from doing so.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
